Subject: [HOTFIX-B] Prevent synchronous I/O blocking in data path
From: Alex Chen <achen@dataflow.internal>
Date: Tue, 19 Nov 2024 11:15:00 -0800

Add O_NONBLOCK flag to the data loader file descriptor to prevent
synchronous blocking during I/O operations. This should resolve the
remaining flush_to_disk latency issue by preventing the data path
from stalling on slow disk I/O.

---
 src/data_loader.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/data_loader.c
+++ b/src/data_loader.c
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ int open_stream(struct stream_ctx *ctx, const char *path)
 {
     init_buffer(ctx);
-    ctx->fd = open(path, O_RDONLY);
+    ctx->fd = open(path, O_RDONLY | O_NONBLOCK);
     if (ctx->fd < 0) {
         fprintf(stderr, "ERROR: cannot open %s\n", path);
         return -1;
